[sander@cwi.nl (Sander Plomp) writes:]
[] Some time ago my girlfriend lost her best game ever due to a panic. She
[] didn't like it. I do not remember what caused the panic, and it is not
[] important. Given the complexity of Nethack there will always be bugs,
[] and panics will remain the most dangerous monster in the game.
[]
[] But I want to be able to recover after a panic.  [...]

when the game "panic"s, it tries to gracefully create an error
save file which is typically equivalent to a save file with ".e"
appended to it.

the error save may still contain the bug that caused the panic
but typically restarting the game is not a problem.

your game maintainer can re-install the error save file by simply
removing the ".e" suffix (in most cases).

